      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The extension's main entry, $3000 (SYSTEM, then /12288): reserves its workspace\n(EXT_RESERVE_WS) and goes on at EXT_KEYB_SETUP with the cursor's blink on. The first of\nthree 3-byte entries at EXT_ON, EXT_ON_AGAIN and EXT_ON_DISPLAY; a fourth is at\nEXT_ON_NO_BLINK.\nObserved: the screen is cleared and shows READY; Series II prints no message."},
        "33": {"synopsis":"Switches the keyboard driver over, with the cursor's blink on (A = 0):\n1. IY+6 = A (the blink flag), IY+1 to IY+5 = 0 (no key held).\n2. Clears the screen (CLS_CMD); Series II prints no message.\n3. The keyboard block's driver ($4016) = ACCENT_KEY_DRV, which wraps EXT_KEY_DRIVER.\n4. On at EXT_ON_DISPLAY for the display driver and the RST $10 hook.\nEntry: IY = the workspace.\nObserved: $4016 = ACCENT_KEY_DRV ($303A) afterwards."},
        "43": {"synopsis":"EXT_KEYB_SETUP: zeroes IY+1 to IY+5, one per pass.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "44": {"comment":"Zero it"},
        "47": {"comment":"Clear the screen; no message on Series II"},
        "50": {"comment":"HL = ACCENT_KEY_DRV"},
        "53": {"comment":"The keyboard block's driver"},
        "56": {"comment":"On to the display driver"},
        "58": {"synopsis":"The keyboard's driver on Series II (the keyboard block's driver at $4016, set by\nEXT_KEYB_SETUP): the CLEAR key becomes the accent key.\n1. A key from EXT_KEY_DRIVER.\n2. CLEAR on its own ($1F) gives no key (A = 0, through BASIC's $2106).\n3. A key that is one of the 9 in ACCENT_TABLE, while CLEAR is held ($3840 bit 1), becomes the\n   byte 10 further on: A, a, E, e, U, u, O, o become the codes of Series II's Á, á, É, é, Ü,\n   ü, Ö, ö glyphs ($5D, $7D, $40, $60, $5E, $7E, $5C, $7C), and BREAK ($01) becomes $1F, the\n   clear-screen code.\n4. Any other key is passed on as it is.\nExit: A = the code, 0 for none.\nObserved: CLEAR held with A, then E, typed $5D and $40; a plain O typed $4F; CLEAR alone typed\nnothing.","comment":"A key from the Series I driver"},
        "61": {"comment":"CLEAR on its own?"},
        "63": {"comment":"Yes: no key (XOR A / RET)"},
        "66": {"comment":"Is it one of the 9 keys of ACCENT_TABLE?"},
        "74": {"comment":"No: HL is past them, at the $00"},
        "76": {"comment":"HL = the matching key"},
        "77": {"comment":"Row 6: is CLEAR held (bit 1)?"},
        "86": {"comment":"No: A = 0, then the key itself"},
        "88": {"comment":"Yes: its accented code, 10 bytes on"},
        "89": {"comment":"A = 0, so A becomes that byte"},
        "90": {"synopsis":"ACCENT_KEY_DRV's end: A + (HL). A = 0 with HL at the key or its accented code gives that\nbyte; after a failed search HL is at the $00 that ends the keys, so A stays the key.","comment":"The code"},
        "1493": {"synopsis":"RENUM_INSERT: the new end, a byte per pass.","comment":"The end up"},
        "1494": {"comment":"B times"},
        "1496": {"comment":"The new end"},
        "1499": {"comment":"BC = the place"},
        "1501": {"comment":"Keep the new end"},
        "1502": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "1503": {"comment":"Bytes from the place to the new end"},
        "1505": {"comment":"As the count"},
        "1507": {"comment":"With the last"},
        "1508": {"comment":"HL = the new end"},
        "1509": {"comment":"HL = the old end, DE = the new end"},
        "1510": {"comment":"Move them up"},
        "1512": {"comment":"The registers back"},
        "1516": {"synopsis":"The accent table ACCENT_KEY_DRV searches (CPIR over 9 bytes):\n- $05EC: the keys A a E e U u O o and $01 (BREAK), then $00, which leaves an unmatched key\n  as it is.\n- $05F6, 10 bytes on: what each becomes with CLEAR held: $5D $7D $40 $60 $5E $7E $5C $7C\n  (Á á É é Ü ü Ö ö in Series II's glyphs) and $1F (clear the screen).\nSeries I has $FF filler here."},
        "1535": {"synopsis":"$FF filler to the end of the ROM."}
      }
    }
  },
